== Trivia ==
* {{dlc+|a}} When {{i|Head of the Keeper}} is picked up as {{c|Keeper}}, he will look similar to the Greed Gaper.{{dlc-}}
* The appearance of Cyclopias is reminiscent of [[wikipedia:Cyclopia|the fatal birth defect of the same name]], which is characterized by the failure of the embryonic prosencephalon to properly divide the orbit of the eyes into two cavities.
* {{dlc+|a+nr}} A {{e|Stoney}} makes the same sound as a Large [[Champion]] Gaper.{{dlc-}}
* Frowning Gapers and Nulls don't make noises until they open their eyes.
* {{dlc|a}} Greed Gapers are also known as Greedlings, a name given by a card of it from ''[[wikipedia:The Binding of Isaac: Four Souls|The Binding of Isaac: Four Souls]]'', although it's seldom referred to as a "Greedling" by players.
* Gapers have among the most variations of any 'family' of monster.
* {{dlc+|r}} Blurbs spawned outside of {{s|Downpour}} will be skin-toned.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc|r}} Wraiths spawned in rooms without water will appear translucent.
* {{dlc|r}} [[Anti:Blurb|Blurbs]], [[Anti:Tidal Gaper|Deep Gapers]], [[Anti:Wraith|Wraiths]], [[Anti:Rotten Gaper|Rotten Gapers]], and [[Anti:Twitchy|Twitchies]] originate from the ''Antibirth'' mod. In ''Antibirth'', Deep Gapers were referred to as Tidal Gapers.
* {{dlc+|r}} Despite being a hybrid with a Trite, Twitchies aren't affected by {{I|Bursting Sack}} due to being categorized as a Gaper variant.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|r}} 34 Dead Isaacs are specifically spawned in {{e|Mother}}'s attack, referencing the 34 playable characters, implying that they are all dead. This makes sense, as all characters really are Isaac himself, whom we see suffocating in a chest in [[Endings#Ending 20/Final Ending|Ending 20]].{{dlc-}}
* A Frowning Gaper figure can be seen in a screenshot for the player's house in [https://store.steampowered.com/app/686060/Mewgenics/ Mewgenics], another game from Edmund McMillen.

